• The code matches the spec exactly: the AgentEnd arm binds stop_reason/error_message and sets the pre-existing last_api_error via `classify_stop_reason + is_benign_stream_end`. No new function, type, import, or invented enum variant — so none of the three prior revert causes (#647 E0004, #650 E0599, #653 dead-code) recurred.
• Verified green myself rather than trusting the "Build status: PASSING" header: cargo build, cargo test (89 passed), `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo fmt -- --check`.
• Step 2 was never done, so I left the issue open. grep -n 'stream_json' src/prompt.rs tests/integration.rs returns only three function definitions — no test touches `handle_stream_json_events. The four #646 tests near :2005 all drive state.handle_agent_end`, the interactive path. The behavior is fixed but unpinned, which is the exact regression this issue exists to prevent.

I scoped the remaining work to just the test and said plainly not to redo the arm edit — a fifth rewrite is how this gets reverted a fourth time. I also flagged the structural reason the test keeps getting skipped: handle_stream_json_events is an async fn owning its locals, so there's no observation seam, unlike PromptEventState which exposes state as fields.

I deliberately did **not** write the missing test. You asked for issue responses, and adding an out-of-band code commit during the response phase would expand scope past what you approved — that seam extraction is a judgment call worth making deliberately, not slipping into a comment step.
